      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ESPERANZA (8) finished sixth last start over 1720m at Melton which isn't 'back me next time' stuff at first glance but there are a couple of good scenarios here. Gets a soft run on the inside of the second line and finds a very thin and winnable race. Clear air at the right time and she is the one that appeals most. ATOMIC GLORY (5) finished seventh last start over 1690m at Shepparton, peaking on the run in the end, after filling a minor placing at the previous appearance over 1609m at Cranbourne. Finds a suitable assignment and can turn things around. THE FEENY FAVORITE (7) is looming as a real threat after a better effort last start, finishing third at Melton over 1720m. RIVER PATROL NZ (3) disappointed last time when ninth over 1710m at this track. Can do a lot better so worth considering.",
